menu "Sensor Provider"

    config MQ135_GPIO
        int "GPIO of the MQ-135 output divider (gas_1; -1: simulated)"
        range -1 48
        default 8
        help
            ADC1 pin (GPIO1-10 on the ESP32-S3). The module is fed from 5 V and its analog
            output (AO) can reach 5 V: never connect it straight to the pin, use the divider below
            (and 100 nF from the pin to GND).

    config MQ135_DIVIDER_TOP_OHMS
        int "Divider resistor from AO to the GPIO (ohms)"
        range 1000 100000
        default 10000

    config MQ135_DIVIDER_BOTTOM_OHMS
        int "Divider resistor from the GPIO to GND (ohms)"
        range 1000 100000
        default 20000
        help
            With 10 k / 20 k the pin sees 2/3 of AO, up to 3.3 V at 5 V; the ADC saturates a bit
            earlier, which only happens with a gas level far above the sensor's range.

    config MQ135_LOAD_RESISTOR_OHMS
        int "Load resistor RL of the module (ohms)"
        range 100 1000000
        default 10000
        help
            Printed next to the SMD resistor of the module near the sensor: 102 = 1 kOhm,
            103 = 10 kOhm. Some modules have a trimmer instead; measure it.

    config MQ135_R0_OHMS
        int "R0: sensor resistance in clean air (ohms)"
        range 1000 10000000
        default 76630
        help
            Calibrate it: after at least 24 h of preheating, leave the sensor in fresh air (about
            400 ppm CO2) and set R0 to the "gas_1: Rs" value of the sensor_provider debug log (esp_log_level_set). The
            default is only a typical value.

    config LM35_GPIO
        int "GPIO of the LM35 output (temperature_2; -1: simulated)"
        range -1 48
        default 5
        help
            ADC1 pin (GPIO1-10 on the ESP32-S3): ADC2 cannot be read while Wi-Fi is active.
            Power the LM35 from 5 V (it needs at least 4 V): its output stays below 1.5 V
            up to 150 degC, safe for the ADC. 10 mV per degree Celsius.

    config LDR_GPIO
        int "GPIO of the first LDR divider (luminosity_1; -1: simulated)"
        range -1 48
        default 4
        help
            ADC1 pin (GPIO1-10 on the ESP32-S3): ADC2 cannot be read while Wi-Fi is active.

    config LDR_2_GPIO
        int "GPIO of the second LDR divider (luminosity_2; -1: simulated)"
        range -1 48
        default -1
        help
            Same divider values as the first LDR. ADC1 pin (GPIO1-10 on the ESP32-S3).

    config LDR_TO_SUPPLY
        bool "LDR between 3.3 V and the GPIO (fixed resistor to GND)"
        default y
        help
            With this wiring the voltage rises with light. Disable it if the LDR goes from the
            GPIO to GND (fixed resistor to 3.3 V).

    config LDR_FIXED_RESISTOR_OHMS
        int "Fixed resistor of the divider (ohms)"
        range 100 1000000
        default 10000

    config LDR_RESISTANCE_AT_10_LUX_OHMS
        int "LDR resistance at 10 lux (ohms, datasheet)"
        range 100 1000000
        default 10000
        help
            GL55xx parts: about 8-20 kOhm at 10 lux.

    config LDR_GAMMA_X100
        int "LDR gamma x 100 (datasheet)"
        range 10 200
        default 70
        help
            Slope of log(R) against log(lux); GL55xx parts: 0.6-0.8.

endmenu
